# Density Compare
# Platinum (Pt) — real density 21.45 g/cm³. equal masses: Platinum vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Platinum Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 7.2mm color: #d0d0e0 at (-20mm, 3.6mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 171.1 g — the water cube is the reference
